{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.CuspShapeBarParity"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.amplification_le_of_barOdd_sq_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.amplification_le_of_barOdd_sq_ge","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.lean#L121-L133","doc":"**Contrapositive — the anchor-smoothness bound.** Away from the compact locus\n(`(barOdd q)² ≥ δ > 0`), the deformation-magnitude amplification is bounded:\n`(barEven q / barOdd q)² ≤ 1 + 4/δ`. At the substrate `δ ≈ (barOdd q₀)² ≈ 0.0437`\nthis gives `≤ 1 + 91.5 ≈ 92.5`, `ρ ≤ 9.62 = O(10)` — far below the `O(10⁶)` the\nc₃ swing demands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.barOdd_sq_le_of_amplification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.barOdd_sq_le_of_amplification","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.lean#L103-L119","doc":"**A large deformation-magnitude amplification forces the compact locus.**\nOver `ℝ`: if the amplification `ρ = |barEven q / barOdd q|` reaches a threshold\n`N > 1` (`N² ≤ ρ²`) then `(barOdd q)² ≤ 4/(N²−1)`. So a big magnitude\namplification requires `|barOdd q|` small, i.e. `q` close to the compact /\nroot-of-unity locus `barOdd = 0` (`q = ±1`). This is the exact statement that the\nholonomy-deformation magnitude is anchor-smooth wherever `q` is bounded away from\n`±1` — in particular at the substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.11`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.sensitivity_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.sensitivity_sq","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MeridianHolonomyAnchorCarrier.lean#L90-L101","doc":"**Boost-hyperbola sensitivity identity.** The logarithmic `q`-sensitivity of\nthe bar-odd meridian-deformation shape `barOdd q = q − q⁻¹` is the ratio\n`barEven q / barOdd q` (`d(barOdd q)/d(log q) = barEven q`); its SQUARE is pinned\nexactly by the boost hyperbola `barEven² − barOdd² = 4` to\n`1 + 4/(barOdd q)²`. Generic field, no archimedean structure (§7c). ","signatureChunk":0}]}